WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.255
Today is October 01, 2026.

3
00:00:07.255 --> 00:00:15.773
Overnight, Wall Street closed a choppy session as the Standard and Poor's five hundred fell nineteen points to test its fifty-day moving average.

4
00:00:15.773 --> 00:00:21.949
The tech-heavy Nasdaq added sixty-three points, while the Dow dropped for a fifth consecutive week.

5
00:00:21.949 --> 00:00:25.846
Treasury yields remain the primary macro battleground.

6
00:00:25.846 --> 00:00:33.248
The benchmark ten-year note touched five point three percent, and the thirty-year bond surged to five point six percent.

7
00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:39.547
Kevin Warsh removed long-standing forward guidance, stripping the bond market of its policy anchor.

8
00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:46.741
Meanwhile, headline August core personal consumption expenditures cooled to three point zero percent year-over-year.

9
00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:53.518
Yet this decline stemmed partly from statistical methodology changes by the Bureau of Economic Analysis.

10
00:00:53.518 --> 00:01:00.319
Adjustments to portfolio management fees alone shaved roughly zero point three percentage points off the print.

11
00:01:00.319 --> 00:01:03.726
Labor resilience further complicates the picture.

12
00:01:03.726 --> 00:01:11.116
Private payrolls rebounded by ninety thousand jobs, beating expectations and halting three months of deceleration.

13
00:01:11.116 --> 00:01:18.530
Interest rate futures now price only a thirty-seven percent chance of an October rate hike, shifting focus to December.

14
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:22.341
Institutional positioning reveals deep crosscurrents.

15
00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:28.125
Large pension funds sold thirty-three billion dollars of equities in end-of-quarter rebalancing.

16
00:01:28.125 --> 00:01:35.050
Simultaneously, systematic trend-following funds provided an offset, preventing a broader breakdown.

17
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:42.451
Turning to tech and industry capital flows, the White House formally rebranded artificial intelligence as Super Intelligence.

18
00:01:42.451 --> 00:01:48.358
Tech titans signed a voluntary frontier safety pact, though it lacks statutory enforcement.

19
00:01:48.358 --> 00:01:51.888
Capital expenditures show no sign of fatigue.

20
00:01:51.888 --> 00:01:58.260
Anthropic disclosed five hundred eighteen billion dollars in planned compute procurement over the next decade.

21
00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:04.670
Autonomous personal agents like Meta Muse and OpenAI Dot are driving structural platform shifts.

22
00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:08.885
These autonomous agents threaten traditional software tollbooths.

23
00:02:08.885 --> 00:02:15.160
If agents bypass individual applications, App Store commission models face severe disruption.

24
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:22.819
In individual equities, Micron Technology, ticker M-U, reported blowout quarterly earnings after the closing bell.

25
00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:31.520
Revenue surged nearly four-fold to over fifty-four billion dollars, and adjusted earnings per share reached thirty-three dollars and forty-two cents.

26
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:39.768
Forward guidance calls for sequential revenue expansion throughout fiscal twenty-twenty-seven, backed by massive high-bandwidth memory demand.

27
00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:44.375
However, Micron stock sold off modestly in extended trading.

28
00:02:44.375 --> 00:02:51.177
Capital expenditures will exceed forty billion dollars next year, sparking classic cyclical peak concerns.

29
00:02:51.177 --> 00:02:57.905
Trading at a single-digit price-to-earnings multiple, Micron faces intense resistance at its recent highs.

30
00:02:57.905 --> 00:03:03.395
Bulls need to defend the two hundred-day moving average to keep the long-term uptrend intact.

31
00:03:03.395 --> 00:03:08.701
Constellation Energy, ticker C-E-G, swung violently during the session.

32
00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:15.197
Shares tumbled six percent intraday on regulatory delays and fears of agent-driven utility switching.

33
00:03:15.197 --> 00:03:24.841
After hours, Constellation announced a twenty-year nuclear supply contract with Amazon Web Services, driving three billion dollars in generation investment.

34
00:03:24.841 --> 00:03:32.660
Resistance sits near its recent consolidation highs, with twenty-day moving average support acting as a critical risk threshold.

35
00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:40.491
Boeing, ticker B-A, secured the multi-billion-dollar Navy sixth-generation fighter development contract over Northrop Grumman.

36
00:03:40.491 --> 00:03:47.035
Following its earlier Air Force F-forty-seven award, Boeing has locked down defense procurement dominance.

37
00:03:47.035 --> 00:03:54.547
Shares gave back early gains in a classic sell-the-news reaction, testing major support at its fifty-day moving average.

38
00:03:54.547 --> 00:04:01.974
All eyes now turn to Friday's non-farm payrolls to confirm whether labor strength can sustain current asset valuations.

39
00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:05.981
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

40
00:04:05.981 --> 00:04:10.148
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
